WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.910 --> 00:00:03.080
This environment was Ready.

2
00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:04.600
It was Deployable.

3
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.440
And it held no reference data at all.

4
00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:11.400
Six minutes and one command later:

5
00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:17.470
80,103 records. Ready is

6
00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:18.360
not loaded.

7
00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:28.922
Service path. Ready is not loaded.

8
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:33.086
What does a new environment
hold, and does ingestion work?

9
00:00:34.668 --> 00:00:37.758
You waited for Deployable when
you brought the environment up.

10
00:00:37.988 --> 00:00:41.838
Bring-up registers the schemas,
and writes no records.

11
00:00:42.228 --> 00:00:45.268
Reference data, from the
community's data definitions,

12
00:00:45.268 --> 00:00:48.948
is loaded by nothing
until you run spi load.

13
00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:54.318
And spi load refuses to start until
the environment is Deployable.

14
00:00:56.616 --> 00:00:59.816
spi load created one
Job for the partition,

15
00:00:59.816 --> 00:01:05.106
and wrote 80,103 records, none
failed, in about six minutes.

16
00:01:05.256 --> 00:01:07.666
Complete means Storage accepted them.

17
00:01:08.376 --> 00:01:10.866
The indexer may still be working.

18
00:01:13.276 --> 00:01:16.126
Deployable does not wait
for the DAGs to register,

19
00:01:16.196 --> 00:01:18.606
so prove ingestion rather than assume it.

20
00:01:18.996 --> 00:01:22.766
You start a run with your own token,
and each task writes on behalf of you.

21
00:01:23.236 --> 00:01:26.726
The editor role you set earlier
lets the stack act for you.

22
00:01:27.396 --> 00:01:31.246
So the stored record's createUser
is you, not the platform.

23
00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.600
One command proves it:

24
00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:37.970
spi test dags, as me.

25
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.640
It checks that it can run.

26
00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:43.250
It runs Echo and an ingest,
and reads the record back.

27
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.480
With --report, the evidence
lands on one page,

28
00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:49.330
and createUser is you.

29
00:01:52.484 --> 00:01:53.644
An easy mistake:

30
00:01:53.644 --> 00:01:56.694
it's Deployable, so the data is there.

31
00:01:56.924 --> 00:01:59.894
Deployable says the
environment can take a deploy.

32
00:02:00.204 --> 00:02:05.094
Reference data is a separate load, and
a load never changes either verdict.

33
00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:08.774
So a search suite on a fresh
environment can find nothing,

34
00:02:08.844 --> 00:02:11.894
and nothing says why,
unless you read the loads.

35
00:02:12.124 --> 00:02:15.894
Check with spi load --status.

36
00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:19.650
So now you can say:

37
00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:23.410
a Deployable environment
holds schemas, not records,

38
00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.850
and ingestion writes
as whoever started it.

39
00:02:29.368 --> 00:02:32.258
Next: which commit does each service run?

